meta {
  name: Verify OTP
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/client/auth/verify-otp
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
  X-Locale: {{locale}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "phone": "{{phone}}",
    "code": "{{otp}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    bru.setVar("token", res.body.token);
  }
}

docs {
  # Verify OTP

  Verifies the code and auto-registers the account on first sign-in. Returns a
  Sanctum token named `mobile-client` — **the only token in the system**. It
  authenticates the client endpoints straight away and the master endpoints as
  soon as the account carries an approved, subscribed master profile.

  The script saves it to the `token` variable used by every other request here.

  **Response 200:**
  ```json
  {
    "token": "1|...",
    "is_new": true,
    "client": {
      "id": 1,
      "name": null,
      "phone": "+99361111222",
      "city_id": null,
      "master_status": null,
      "master_id": null,
      "has_master_access": false,
      "created_at": "2026-08-15 10:00:00"
    }
  }
  ```

  **Routing the app right after sign-in:**

  | Field               | Value        | Screen to open                       |
  |---------------------|--------------|--------------------------------------|
  | `is_new`            | `true`       | Profile setup (name + city)          |
  | `master_status`     | `null`       | Client mode, offer "become a master" |
  | `master_status`     | `pending`    | "Application under review"           |
  | `master_status`     | `rejected`   | Rejection reason + re-apply          |
  | `has_master_access` | `true`       | Role switch is available             |

  `master_status` may be `approved` while `has_master_access` is `false` — the
  profile is approved but the subscription has lapsed or is not issued yet.

  **Errors:**
  - `422` — invalid or expired OTP
}
